/P 94 0 R
/E (Dr Karthik Raman has been revolutionising the field of systems biology through computational research at IIT Madras. One of the most prominent projects carried out under his supervision was the development of the computational framework CO-FSEOF \(Co production flux scanning based on enforced objective flux\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11 12]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (This framework guides scientists in identifying optimal genetic interventions of microbes to produce more than one desirable metabolites in a single computational run and also improves carbon utilisation. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13 14]
>>
endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (This model is based on flux balance analysis \(FBA\) to predict flux distributions in a genome-scale metabolic model \(GSMM\) of a microbe \(E. coli & S. cerevisiae\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [15 16]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (Earlier, the FSEOF model optimised microbes for only one metabolite at a time, making the process computationally expensive and inefficient to scale. Co-FSEOF, therefore, represents a step forward toward sustainable and efficient bioprocessing.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [17]
>>
